+# Native parametric family — mapped-region relay
+
+This family preserves the two-row-legend task as its exact default and adds one
+opt-in sequential setting:
+
+- `canonical` applies the selected canonical Racket program byte-for-byte.
+- `mapped_region_relay` applies that legend mapping, counts the resulting
+  colour-2 connected regions to the left of a colour-9 separator, and uses the
+  count (1, 2, or 3) to choose one of three ordered colour-6 payloads to recolour
+  to 8.
+
+The controller always contains three disconnected raw colour-1 components.
+Colour-2 bridges join them only after the legend maps 1→2, so a retained
+counterfactual that counts raw source components always chooses payload 3.  The
+qualified 30×30 witness has mapped count 2 and therefore changes under that
+ablation.
+
+Inputs are matched across settings.  The adapter independently accepts 2–6
+demonstrations and 1–4 prefix-stable queries.  The first two demonstrations
+have equal dimensions, legend placement, source area, and total occupancy but
+require different intermediate values, blocking nuisance lookup shortcuts.
+
+`verify.py` runs the bounded named-rival and protected-Racket audit;
+`promotion.json` is the native adapter contract; source-bound evidence is under
+`evidence/`.  Qualification and causal replay receipts are stored outside the
+source closure under `WORK/checks/69cab6228fdc/`.
